{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Relation Extraction & Knowledge Graph Construction Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: pattern-based extraction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "PATTERNS = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (r\"(?P<s>[A-Z]\\w+) (?:is|was) (?:a|an|the) (?P<o>[A-Z]?\\w+)\", \"isA\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (r\"(?P<s>[A-Z]\\w+) (?:is|was) born in (?P<o>\\w+)\", \"bornIn\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (r\"(?P<s>[A-Z]\\w+) works? (?:at|for) (?P<o>[A-Z]\\w+)\", \"worksAt\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    (r\"(?P<s>[A-Z]\\w+) founded (?P<o>[A-Z]\\w+)\", \"founded\"),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "See `code/main.py` for the full toy extractor. Hearst patterns still ship in domain-specific pipelines because they are debuggable."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: supervised relation classification"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForSequenceClassification"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tok = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(\"Babelscape/rebel-large\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = AutoModelForSequenceClassification.from_pretrained(\"Babelscape/rebel-large\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "text = \"Tim Cook was born in Alabama. He later became CEO of Apple.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "encoded = tok(text, return_tensors=\"pt\", truncation=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "output = model.generate(**encoded, max_length=200)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "triples = tok.batch_decode(output, skip_special_tokens=False)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "REBEL is a seq2seq relation extractor: text in, triples out, already in Wikidata property ids. Fine-tuned on distant-supervision data. Standard open-weights baseline."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: LLM-prompted extraction with anchoring"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "prompt = f\"\"\"Extract (subject, relation, object) triples from the text."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For each triple, include the exact character span in the source text."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Text: {text}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Output JSON:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "[{{\"subject\": {{\"text\": \"...\", \"span\": [start, end]}},"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "   \"relation\": \"...\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "   \"object\": {{\"text\": \"...\", \"span\": [start, end]}}}}, ...]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Only include triples fully supported by the text. No inference beyond what is stated."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "\"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Verify every returned span against the source. Reject anything where `text[start:end] != triple_entity`. This is the AEVS \"verify\" step in its minimal form."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: canonicalize onto a closed ontology"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "RELATION_MAP = {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"is the CEO of\": \"P169\",       # \"chief executive officer\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"was born in\":   \"P19\",         # \"place of birth\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"founded\":        \"P112\",       # \"founded by\" (inverted subject/object)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"works at\":       \"P108\",       # \"employer\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def canonicalize(relation):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rel_low = relation.lower().strip()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if rel_low in RELATION_MAP:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return RELATION_MAP[rel_low]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return None   # drop unmapped open relations or route to manual review"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Canonicalization is often 60-80% of the engineering work. Budget for it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: build a small graph and query"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "triples = extract(text)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "graph = {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for s, r, o in triples:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    graph.setdefault(s, []).append((r, o))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def neighbors(node, relation=None):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [(r, o) for r, o in graph.get(node, []) if relation is None or r == relation]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(neighbors(\"Tim Cook\", relation=\"P108\"))    # -> [(P108, Apple)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This is the atom of every RAG-over-KG system. Scale it with RDF triple stores (Blazegraph, Virtuoso), property graphs (Neo4j), or vector-augmented graph stores."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run the pattern extractor in `code/main.py` on 5 news-article sentences. Hand-check precision.\n2. **Medium.** Use REBEL (or a small LLM) on the same sentences. Compare triples. Which extractor has higher precision? Higher recall?\n3. **Hard.** Build the AEVS pipeline: extract with LLM + verify spans against source. Measure hallucination rate before vs after the verify step on 50 Wikipedia-style sentences."
      ]
    }
